wwv_flow_imp_page.create_page_plug(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(124574423445736940319)
,p_plug_name=>'PL/SQL Basics'
,p_region_template_options=>'#DEFAULT#:t-Region--scrollBody'
,p_plug_template=>4072358936313175081
,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<!-- ========================= PL/SQL MODULE 1 : BASICS ========================= -->',
'',
'<!-- <h2>Module 1: PL/SQL Basics</h2> -->',
'',
'<p>',
'<b>PL/SQL</b> stands for <b>Procedural Language / Structured Query Language</b>.',
unistr('It is Oracle\2019s extension of SQL that allows us to write'),
'<b>procedural code</b> inside the database.',
'</p>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h3>1. Introduction to PL/SQL</h3>',
'',
'<p>',
'PL/SQL is a block-structured programming language that combines',
'<b>SQL statements</b> with <b>procedural features</b> like conditions and loops.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>',
'It is mainly used to write business logic directly inside the database.',
'</p>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h3>2. Advantages of PL/SQL</h3>',
'',
'<ul>',
'  <li>Improves performance by reducing network traffic</li>',
'  <li>Supports variables, loops, and conditions</li>',
'  <li>Better security for database logic</li>',
'  <li>Easy integration with SQL</li>',
'  <li>Reusable code using procedures and functions</li>',
'</ul>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h3>3. PL/SQL Architecture</h3>',
'',
'<p>',
'PL/SQL code is processed by the <b>PL/SQL Engine</b>.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>',
'If the code contains SQL statements, they are passed to the',
'<b>SQL Engine</b>. Procedural statements are handled by the PL/SQL Engine itself.',
'</p>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h3>4. PL/SQL Block Structure</h3>',
'',
'<p>',
'A PL/SQL program is written in blocks.',
'Each block has three sections:',
'</p>',
'',
'<ul>',
unistr('  <li><b>DECLARE</b> \2013 Used to declare variables (optional)</li>'),
unistr('  <li><b>BEGIN</b> \2013 Contains executable statements (mandatory)</li>'),
unistr('  <li><b>EXCEPTION</b> \2013 Handles errors (optional)</li>'),
'</ul>',
'',
'<b>Syntax:</b>',
'<pre>',
'DECLARE',
'  -- variable declarations',
'BEGIN',
'  -- executable statements',
'EXCEPTION',
'  -- error handling',
'END;',
'</pre>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h3>5. Types of PL/SQL Blocks</h3>',
'',
'<p>',
'There are three types of PL/SQL blocks:',
'</p>',
'',
'<ol>',
unistr('  <li><b>Anonymous Block</b> \2013 Written and executed once</li>'),
unistr('  <li><b>Procedure</b> \2013 Stored program that performs an action</li>'),
unistr('  <li><b>Function</b> \2013 Stored program that returns a value</li>'),
'</ol>',
'',
'<p>',
'Among these, <b>Anonymous Blocks</b> are mainly used for learning and testing.',
'</p>',
'',
'<hr>',
'',
'<h2>In Simple Words</h2>',
'',
'<p>',
'<b>PL/SQL</b> allows us to write logic inside the database using SQL + programming features.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>',
'<b>Module 1</b> explains what PL/SQL is, why it is used,',
'how it works internally, and the basic structure of PL/SQL programs.',
'</p>',
''))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
  'expand_shortcuts', 'N',
  'output_as', 'HTML')).to_clob
);
end;
/
